# What is excluded here, and why each one is deliberate:
#
# - tests/<name>/ holds field notes from adopting a project: internal, short-lived, and
#   never committed, by Costin's ruling (d-tests-folders-never-committed). Ignored here so
#   that is a check rather than a thing to remember. `git add -f` still bypasses it.
#   Anything worth keeping from one is harvested into docs/CONCERNS.yaml instead.
# - Python bytecode from scripts/.
# - The three artifacts Rite COPIES out of ~/.claude — mirrored memory, plan copies and session
#   scripts. They are written on every session and kept on disk, where the checker still grades
#   them; they are simply not pushed. This is the same default /rite:init now seeds into a new
#   project, and this repository follows it rather than exempting itself.
#
#   IT SAID THE OPPOSITE UNTIL 2026-09-19, and the reversal was paid for rather than argued.
#   These lines read: "docs/claude-memory.md is generated by the memory-mirror hook and MUST be
#   tracked. It exists precisely so agent memory is auditable from the repo; ignoring it would
#   restore the problem it was created to solve." That ruling was deliberate, reasoned, and made
#   by the author of the standard — and it published his SSH host aliases, private-key filenames
#   and second GitHub account to a public repository, automatically, on every memory change.
#   Auditability is served by the copy EXISTING, never by its being pushed. The full reasoning,
#   including what the traffic measurement showed, is in d-agent-copies-default-untracked.
#
# - spec/PROJECT-STANDARD.md and spec/SESSION-PROTOCOL.md are GENERATED but MUST be tracked.
#   They are the readable form of the spec, and the drift gate compares the committed file
#   against a fresh render — an untracked generated file could never drift, which would
#   silently disable the check. Note the distinction from the three above: those are copies of
#   PRIVATE state, these are renderings of a file already in the repo.
/tests/*/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
docs/claude-memory.md
docs/PLAN-*.md
docs/session-scripts/
